[gd_scene load_steps=25 format=3]

; zone_catacombs — the floor tower (WLD-07), band 19–23.
;
; Nine floors, one footprint. Every floor is the same forty-metre room at a different depth,
; stacked twenty-four metres apart, and only the one the player is standing on is awake. That
; is a deliberate trade: the variety in a tower is meant to come from what each floor ASKS,
; not from what it looks like (FR-7.12, doc 02 §10.1). Nine hand-carved rooms asking the same
; question would still be one floor nine times.
;
; One scene rather than nine means one navigation bake, one load, and a descent that is a fade
; rather than a loading screen the player sits through eight times on the way to the boss.
;
; What lives here is only what data cannot hold: where the player lands, where the stair is,
; where a pylon may stand and where a wave walks in. Which verb each floor asks, how long its
; clock runs and what it sends is in game/data/zones/act1.json, where the validator can check
; that no two floors in a row ask the same thing.
;
; The exit is on floor one, beside the mouth shrine — you leave the way you came in, and the
; bottom of the tower sends you back up to it.

